# serial_cycle_bypass -- a detour drawn in the document itself, and the
# reason the shape stops being a ring the moment it is drawn.
#
# `serial_cycle_shadow.bron` gave a standby the very regions the domain it
# would replace already holds, and the flow derivation refused it for
# having two writers on one region. This declaration answers that refusal
# honestly: `dogwood` gets regions of its own, so every region here keeps
# exactly one writer and exactly one reader, and the flow derivation is
# perfectly happy.
#
# What it loses instead is the shape. alder now writes to two successors,
# `ask_ab` onward to birch and `ask_ad` onward to dogwood, and cedar reads
# from two predecessors. So alder spans three peers rather than two, and no
# single directed walk visits all four domains once and comes home -- every
# lap that reaches cedar has left somebody out.
#
# The finding this declaration exists to state: a ring with a spare route
# is not a ring with a spare route. It is a different shape, one with a
# choice of laps, and `ring_order` answers null rather than picking one.
#
# Read whole by `caravan/read.rye`; refused by `caravan/standby.rye`.

system serial_cycle_bypass

domain alder
domain birch
domain cedar
domain dogwood

channel alder birch
channel birch cedar
channel cedar alder
channel alder dogwood
channel dogwood cedar

region ask_ab 4096
region ask_bc 4096
region ask_ca 4096
region ask_ad 4096
region ask_dc 4096
region taken 64

grant ask_ab alder rw
grant ask_ab birch r
grant ask_bc birch rw
grant ask_bc cedar r
grant ask_ca cedar rw
grant ask_ca alder r
grant ask_ad alder rw
grant ask_ad dogwood r
grant ask_dc dogwood rw
grant ask_dc cedar r
grant taken alder rw
grant taken cedar r
